'''× ''Beallara''''', abbreviated '''Bllra.''' in the horticultural trade,<ref name=NamesWithAbbreviations>{{citation |url=http://londonorchidsociety.org/RHS/hybrid06.htm |title=Hybrid Genus Names With Abbreviations |publisher=London Orchid Society |author=Julian Shaw (the International Orchid Registrar at the Royal Horticultural Society) |accessdate=23 March 2016 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160402221317/http://londonorchidsociety.org/RHS/hybrid06.htm |archive-date=2 April 2016 |url-status=dead }}</ref> was the [[nothogenus]] for [[intergeneric hybrid]]s between the orchid genera ''[[Brassia]]'', ''Cochlioda'', ''[[Miltonia]]'' and ''Odontoglossum'' (Brs. x Cda. x Milt. x Odm.). As ''Cochlioda'' and ''Odontoglossum'' have been synonymized with ''[[Oncidium]]'', the current genera involved are ''Brassia'' x ''Miltonia'' × ''Oncidium'', so the correct genus name is [[× Aliceara|× ''Aliceara'']].<ref name=RHSList>{{Cite web |date=2017 |title=Alphabetical One-Table List of Genera and Intergeneric Hybrids |publisher=Royal Horticultural Society |url=https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/pdfs/plant-registration-forms/list-of-orchid-genera-with-components.pdf |access-date=2023-12-15 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230323103826/https://www.rhs.org.uk/plants/pdfs/plant-registration-forms/list-of-orchid-genera-with-components.pdf |archive-date=2023-03-23 }}</ref>

==Description==
This plant has a branched stem that grows to about {{convert|150|cm}} in height. The leaves are elongated and lanceolate, reaching about {{convert|60|cm}} of length. The flowers are numerous, about 14 to 16, and last long, between 20 and 30 days. It has fleshy large pseudobulbs. These orchids are commonly cultivated in greenhouses for ornamental purposes, resulting in a huge variety of cultivars of different colors.

